Local vs global faithfulness - formal tests
==============================================================
source: run3/outputs/9_local_steer

Paired Wilcoxon signed-rank on per-example (rho_local - rho_global).
Positive gap = local SHAP ranks that example's effects better.
Wilcoxon and the 95% CI here resample EXAMPLES ONLY and treat them as
independent. They are not (shared features) - quote the crossed table below.

block:kind               local  global     gap            95% CI  wilcoxon p  win frac
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A:importance            +0.351  +0.057  +0.294   [+0.262,+0.326]    1.29e-17     0.970
A:directional           +0.140  +0.132  +0.008   [-0.035,+0.054]    8.10e-01     0.530
B:importance            +0.015  +0.320  -0.305   [-0.371,-0.241]    3.15e-12     0.168
B:directional           +0.187  +0.213  -0.026   [-0.093,+0.040]    5.71e-01     0.484

Crossed (pigeonhole) bootstrap over examples x features, B=1000:
  100 examples share 89 distinct features (mean 29.7 candidates/example, mean pairwise Jaccard 0.70), so the
  per-example gaps are correlated through the features. This resamples both.

block:kind                 gap    crossed 95% CI  crossed p  SE inflation
------------------------------------------------------------------------
A:importance            +0.294   [-0.020,+0.605]      0.064         9.47x
A:directional           +0.008   [-0.343,+0.365]      0.952         8.39x
B:importance            -0.305   [-0.589,+0.059]      0.104         5.02x
B:directional           -0.026   [-0.523,+0.544]      0.896         8.36x
  Mildly conservative: it double-counts interaction variance, and a resampled
  duplicate feature introduces rank ties.

Decomposition of the block [A] importance gap:
  mean active fraction of candidates = 0.498
  gap ~ frac_active            slope=-0.026  R2=0.000  p=8.35e-01
  gap ~ n_active               slope=-0.001  R2=0.000  p=8.68e-01
  gap ~ frac_active + n_cands  coefs=[-0.047, 0.006]  R2=0.002
  A high R2 here means the local-vs-global margin is largely an activity effect,
  not a ranking-quality effect.

Continuous control (partial Spearman | activation magnitude):
  mean partial rho local  = +0.038 (n=100)
  mean partial rho global = -0.168 (n=100)
  paired gap = +0.206  wilcoxon p=6.31e-11
  (examples-only Wilcoxon - same shared-feature dependence as above, so this p
  understates the uncertainty; descriptive only)

